    "Notes Updated": "3/24/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Big fan of Dinges' swing. Think he has to learn to tone it down at times, but there's a ton of bat speed from a relatively simple setup.\n Power is going to be there, I'm convinced of it\n Swing and miss will still likely be an issue early, but I think as he sees more pro pitching he has the approach to squash that\n Main update from the draft report is belief that he can catch\n Have seen pop times in the mid 1.8's and he looked solid catching Miz in the Breakout game, which is not easy\n Athleticism plays back there and the arm can be plus\n Still work to do on receiving/blocking, but the athleticism is going to help him get that done",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/23/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Post Draft Thoughts\n I love Dinges' swing, there's so much power behind it and yet is pretty controlled\n Has potential for some pretty big power\n Swing and miss will likely be an issue early, but I think as he sees more pro pitching he has the approach to squash that\n Drafted as a catcher, very good athlete, will be interesting to see if he can do it",
